<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rojo sees end-1996 inflation round 3.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rojo sees end-1996 inflation round 3.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Spain governor Luis Angel Rojo said on Thursday that final 1996 inflation could be around 3.3 percent, lower than a previous central bank target of around 3.5 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Nineteen-ninety six inflation will be around 3.3 percent,&quot; Rojo told a senate committee.</p>
<p>The government's year-end target is 3.4 percent.</p>
</text>
